Section 6 — Detailed Dry Run
Consider the input string: "NNEESW"

Step	Character	Vertical Counter	Horizontal Counter	Explanation
1	'N'	1	0	Moved North (+1)
2	'N'	2	0	Moved North again (+1)
3	'E'	2	1	Moved East (+1)
4	'E'	2	2	Moved East again (+1)
5	'S'	1	2	Moved South (-1)
6	'W'	1	1	Moved West (-1)
Final net displacement: vertical = +1 (North), horizontal = +1 (East)
Resulting final sense of direction: "North-East"

Section 7 — Edge Cases
Empty string
Input: "" → Expected Output: "Origin"
All same elements (e.g., "NNNN")
Input: "NNNN" → Expected Output: "North"
Array (string) with two elements
Input: "NS" → Expected Output: "Origin"
Contradictory movements with negatives
Input: "EWWE" → Expected Output: "West" (if net horizontal is negative)
Already balanced (e.g., "NESW")
Input: "NESW" → Expected Output: "Origin"
Section 8 — Common Mistakes
Not handling invalid characters in the input string.
• Fix: Either ignore or validate each character before processing.
Forgetting to account for the case when both displacements are zero (i.e., the origin).
• Fix: Use a conditional check after processing the input.
Incorrect concatenation of diagonal directions (e.g., missing a delimiter).
• Fix: Check if one part of the string is empty before concatenation.
Assuming input is non-empty.
• Fix: Handle the edge case when the string is empty.
Overcomplicating the problem by trying to simulate movement step by step unnecessarily.
• Fix: Use net sum of moves for a straightforward solution.
Section 9 — Interview Tips
Explain the cancellation effect (e.g., how north counters south) as soon as you see the problem.
State clearly that you'll count the individual directions and then combine the net results.
Interviewers are testing your ability to simplify a series of instructions and your attention to edge cases.
Follow-up questions may include: "How would you modify this solution for movements with different step lengths?" or "What if additional directions (e.g., Northeast) were allowed?"
• Be ready to discuss how the logic would extend to weighted steps or additional direction codes.
